# Mobily Tech Support System — Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack
- Backend: FastAPI 0.115+ (Python 3.12, Async)
- ORM: SQLAlchemy 2.0 Async + Alembic
- Validation: Pydantic v2
- Frontend: HTMX 2.0 + Alpine.js + Tailwind CSS 4 + Jinja2
- Database: PostgreSQL 16.4
- Cache: Redis 7.2
- Task Queue: Celery 5.4 + Celery Beat
- Real-time: Server-Sent Events (SSE)
- Auth: OAuth2 + JWT RS256 + Argon2id

## Critical Rules — Follow Always
1. ALL text in UI must use t("key", lang=lang) — NEVER hardcode Arabic or English text
2. ALL user-facing DB fields need BOTH _ar AND _en columns (e.g., name_ar, name_en)
3. HTML templates ALWAYS have lang="{{ lang }}" dir="{{ dir }}" on <html> tag
4. Use Tailwind ps/pe/ms/me instead of pl/pr/ml/mr (RTL-safe)
5. ALL database queries use SQLAlchemy async — NEVER raw SQL with user input
6. ALL timestamps use TIMESTAMPTZ (timezone-aware)
7. ALL primary keys are UUID (gen_random_uuid())
8. Soft delete pattern: deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ (never hard delete)
9. Every ticket action creates a ticket_timeline entry (immutable)
10. Every config change creates an audit_log entry (immutable, no delete/update)

## File Structure
- app/api/       → Route handlers
- app/models/    → SQLAlchemy models
- app/schemas/   → Pydantic schemas
- app/services/  → Business logic
- app/i18n/      → ar.json + en.json translations
- app/templates/ → Jinja2 HTML templates
- app/static/    → CSS + JS assets

## Response Format
- Always show the FULL file path before code
- Always show which file to create/modify
- Async functions everywhere (async def)
- Type hints on every function
